course: dictionary
lesson: 46
title: Hard word trap: accommodate
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Accommodate is on the Years 5–6 list of harder words, and it is easy to get wrong. It means to have room for people or things, or to give someone a place to stay. «Each bus accommodates 40 pupils» means each bus has room for 40 pupils.
explain: The word can also mean to help someone by changing plans for them. «Teachers accommodate different needs» means teachers adjust what they do so every child can learn. Ask yourself: is there enough space, or is someone being helped? Try the meaning in the sentence to check.
explain: The spelling is the hard part. «Accommodate has a double c and a double m: A-C-C-O-M-M-O-D-A-T-E.» Say the letters in order out loud, then write them, and check the double letters.
fact: Accommodate means to provide a place for someone, or to have enough space for people or things.
fact: «Most hard words hide a trap» such as a double letter, a silent letter, or a sound people say wrongly.
fact: Accommodate has a double c and a double m: A-C-C-O-M-M-O-D-A-T-E.
fact: The Years 5–6 list in England has about 100 harder words, and accommodate is one of them.
fact: Other words on that list include ancient, necessary, privilege and sufficient.
exercise: «Each bus accommodates 40 pupils.» How many pupils can 2 buses take? | 42 | 400 | 38 | *80
exercise: Which spelling of the word is correct? | acommodate | *accommodate | accomodate | accommodat
exercise: «The hotel can accommodate up to 300 guests.» What does accommodate mean here? | Argues with | Throws out | *Has enough room for | Closes for the winter
test: How many double letters does accommodate have? | 4 | 1 | 3 | *2
test: Teachers try to accommodate different needs. What does accommodate mean here? | Copy exactly | Ignore completely | Shout at | *Help by changing plans to suit
exam: Which sentence uses accommodate correctly? | The door accommodates quickly. | I accommodate my sister's bike. | The hall accommodate 200 people is yesterday. | *The hall can accommodate 200 people.
